error[E0406]: the code `deferred` generates in the right side of `&&` has a `defer`
  --> tests/ui/macro_operand_scope.wid:50:16
   |
50 |   e = false && deferred(true)
   |                ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ `deferred` expands here, in the right side of `&&`
  ::: tests/ui/macro_operand_scope.wid:15:5
   |
15 |     defer puts("deferred ran")
   |     -------------------------- this `defer` would wait for the end of the block around it
   = note: a `defer` runs when its block ends, but code in the right side of `&&` runs only when the left side is true, so the end of the block around it can't tell whether the `defer` was reached
help: call `deferred` in a branch of an `if` instead, whose end runs the `defer`; or, if its code may always run, as a statement of its own before this line (`v = deferred(…)`), and use `v` here
   = see `wid explain E0406`

